1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,365
In 2012,

2
00:00:01,484 --> 00:00:05,207
satellites suddenly counted five times more fire in Bangladesh.

3
00:00:05,657 --> 00:00:07,395
Was the land suddenly burning?

4
00:00:07,445 --> 00:00:09,589
Mostly, NASA just got a sharper camera.

5
00:00:10,039 --> 00:00:13,101
Parallax Fire puts both satellites on one honest scale.

6
00:00:13,361 --> 00:00:14,907
Most of the jump melts away.

7
00:00:15,357 --> 00:00:16,432
Every fire season,

8
00:00:16,552 --> 00:00:17,956
mapped district by district.

9
00:00:18,406 --> 00:00:20,311
Plus today’s hot spots, live,

10
00:00:20,431 --> 00:00:22,484
as five fire satellites pass overhead.

11
00:00:22,934 --> 00:00:23,862
Parallax Fire.

12
00:00:24,122 --> 00:00:26,973
Same fires. Two cameras. One honest record.
